## Cycle 1 (fresh reviewer, 2026-06-12)

Verdict: NEEDS-WORK -> fixed. One Important, two Improvements.

- IMPORTANT (APPLIED) - endpoint.py curl-skeleton bug: the request-body content-type variable `ct` was overwritten by the response-handling block, so the skeleton's multipart guard tested the RESPONSE content-type. For pages-deployment-create-deployment (multipart) the skeleton printed a JSON `-d '<json body>'` body, contradicting the skill's hard rule "deploy a directory with Wrangler, not curl". FIX: captured the request body content-type in a distinct `body_ct` variable and gate the skeleton on it; the skeleton now prints "deploy is a multipart upload - use wrangler" with NO -d body for the deploy op, while create-project/add-domain keep their JSON body. Verified both.
- IMPROVEMENT (not applied) - the skeleton substitutes {account_id} -> $CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID but leaves {project_name}/{deployment_id} literal. Intentional: account_id is the injected env var; the others are per-call args the agent fills.
- IMPROVEMENT (not applied) - sources.md "~10 MB / 1986 paths" vs endpoint.py "10 MB"; harmless, the 1986-paths figure is correctly scoped to sources.md (the upstream full spec).

VERIFY (all clean): priority ops correct vs the bundled Pages slice (create-project name+production_branch required; add-domain name required; get-deployment-info latest_stage; deploy multipart->wrangler); stage enums exact; envelope described + "check success not just HTTP" in 5 places; auth Bearer+CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN+CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID + no-login consistent; account_id treated as non-secret context (not via token-load rule); Wrangler commands real; endpoint.py handles 3.0.3 + path-level param merge; slice self-contained (0 dangling refs); uncertain facts (token-permission UI label, tail filter flags) flagged. All 4 behavioral flows clean.

